96770</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B7"><label>7</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Rastogi</surname><given-names>DP</given-names></name><name><surname>Singh</surname><given-names>VP</given-names></name><name><surname>Singh</surname><given-names>V</given-names></name><name><surname>Dey</surname><given-names>SK</given-names></name><name><surname>Rao</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Homeopathy in HIV infection: a trial report of double-blind placebo controlled study</article-title><source>Br J Homeopath</source><year>1999</year><volume>88</volume><issue>2</issue><fpage>49</fpage><lpage>57</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="B8"><label>8</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Singh</surname><given-names>N</given-names></name><name><surname>Squier</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Sivek</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><article-title>Determinants of non-traditional therapy use in patients with HIV infection</article-title><source>Arch Intern Med</source><year>1996</year><volume>156</volume><fpage>197</fpage><lpage>201</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">8546553</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B9"><label>9</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Ullman</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Controlled clinical trials evaluating the homeopathic treatment of people with human immunodeficiency virus or acquired immune deficiency syndrome</article-title><source>J Altern Complement Med</source><year>2003</year><volume>9</volume><fpage>133</fpage><lpage>41</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12676041</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B10"><label>10</label><citation citation-type="gov"><article-title>Annual Report</article-title><year>2005</year><publisher-name>Ministry of Health and Family Welfare, Government of India</publisher-name></citation></ref><ref id="B11"><label>11</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Leake</surname><given-names>B</given-names></name><name><surname>Nyamathi</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Gelberg</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Reliability, validity and composition of a subset of the CDC AIDS knowledge questionnaire in a sample of homeless and impoverished adults</article-title><source>Med Care</source><year>1997</year><volume>35</volume><fpage>747</fpage><lpage>55</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9268248</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B12"><label>12</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Wahner-Roedler</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name><name><surname>Vincent</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Elkin</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name><name><surname>Loehrer</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name><name><surname>Cha</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Bauer</surname><given-names>B</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Physicians&#x02019; attitudes toward complementary and alternative medicine and their knowledge of specific therapies: a survey at an academic medical center</article-title><source>Evid Based Complement Alternat Med</source><year>2006</year><volume>3</volume><issue>4</issue><fpage>495</fpage><lpage>501</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">17173114</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B13"><label>13</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Marotta</surname><given-names>F</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Complementary and alternative medicine in clinical practice. Complementary and allopathic medicine: the hospital as a place of possible integration</article-title><source>Evid Based Complement Alternat Med</source><year>2006</year><volume>3</volume><issue>4</issue><fpage>549</fpage><lpage>50</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">17173120</pub-id></citation></ref></ref-list></back></article>